ain 2021 (Online) 25th February Evening Shift","nextq":"H9iLe4hN4Na9MbnjaR1kltbsa7r","prevq":"KUZ5uhS8NaNi6g5iLt1kltb3bda","questions":[{"question_id":"J5V2MxZKBw3M7JtYg81kltbjh7x","chapter":"salt-analysis","chapterGroup":"inorganic-chemistry","country":"in","difficulty":"easy","exam":"jee-main","examGroup":"jee","languages":["en","hi"],"marks":4,"negMarks":1,"paperTitle":"JEE Main 2021 (Online) 25th February Evening Shift","permalink":"given-below-are-two-statements-brbrstatement-i--the-jee-main-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-z8xhseqddjvibtto","question":{"en":{"direction":null,"content":"Given below are two statements :<br><br>Statement I : The identification of Ni<sup>2+</sup> is carried out by dimethyl glyoxime in the presence of NH<sub>4</sub>OH. <br><br>Statement II : The dimethyl glyoxime is a bidentate neutral ligand.<br><br>In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below :","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"Statement I is false but Statement II is true."},{"identifier":"B","content":"Statement I is true but Statement II is false."},{"identifier":"C","content":"Both Statement I and Statement II are false."},{"identifier":"D","content":"Both Statement I and Statement II are true."}],"correct_options":["D"],"answer":null,"explanation":"<p><b>Statement I</b> is true. Dimethyl glyoxime (DMG) is a chelating reagent commonly used for the identification of Ni<sup>2+</sup> ions in aqueous solution. In the presence of ammonium hydroxide (NH<sub>4</sub>OH), Ni<sup>2+</sup> reacts with dimethyl glyoxime to form a deep red-colored complex, which can be used to confirm the presence of Ni<sup>2+</sup> ions.</p>\n\n<p><b>Statement II</b> is also true. Dimethyl glyoxime is a neutral bidentate ligand, which means it has two donor atoms that can coordinate with a metal ion, and its overall charge is neutral.</p>\n<img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l3pepyf8/303589cb-2e0e-479b-8a91-9871db081a32/6df4fd30-de43-11ec-a44f-e3762c775e6c/file-1l3pepyf9.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l3pepyf8/303589cb-2e0e-479b-8a91-9871db081a32/6df4fd30-de43-11ec-a44f-e3762c775e6c/file-1l3pepyf9.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Main 2021 (Online) 25th February Evening Shift Chemistry - Salt Analysis Question 40 English Explanation\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l3pepyf8/303589cb-2e0e-479b-8a91-9871db081a32/6df4fd30-de43-11ec-a44f-e3762c775e6c/file-1l3pepyf9.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l3pepyf8/303589cb-2e0e-479b-8a91-9871db081a32/6df4fd30-de43-11ec-a44f-e3762c775e6c/file-1l3pepyf9.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l3pepyf8/303589cb-2e0e-479b-8a91-9871db081a32/6df4fd30-de43-11ec-a44f-e3762c775e6c/file-1l3pepyf9.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l3pepyf8/303589cb-2e0e-479b-8a91-9871db081a32/6df4fd30-de43-11ec-a44f-e3762c775e6c/file-1l3pepyf9.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l3pepyf8/303589cb-2e0e-479b-8a91-9871db081a32/6df4fd30-de43-11ec-a44f-e3762c775e6c/file-1l3pepyf9.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l3pepyf8/303589cb-2e0e-479b-8a91-9871db081a32/6df4fd30-de43-11ec-a44f-e3762c775e6c/file-1l3pepyf9.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\">"},"hi":{"direction":null,"content":"नीचे दिए गए दो कथन हैं :<br><br>कथन I : Ni<sup>2+</sup> की पहचान NH<sub>4</sub>OH की उपस्थिति में डाइमिथाइल ग्लाइऑक्साइम द्वारा की जाती है। <br><br>कथन II : डाइमिथाइल ग्लाइऑक्साइम एक द्विदंत समजाति लिगेंड है।<br><br>उपरोक्त कथनों के आधार पर, नीचे दिए गए विकल्पों में से सही उत्तर चुनें :","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"कथन I गलत है पर कथन II सही है।"},{"identifier":"B","content":"कथन I सही है पर कथन II गलत है।"},{"identifier":"C","content":"कथन I और कथन II दोनों गलत हैं।"},{"identifier":"D","content":"कथन I और कथन II दोनों सही हैं।"}],"correct_options":["D"],"answer":null,"explanation":null,"comprehension":null}},"subject":"chemistry","subjectGroup":null,"timeAllotted":120000,"topic":"systematic-analysis-of-cations","type":"mcq","year":2021,"paperId":"jee-main-2021-online-25th-february-evening-slot","isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"tags":["assertion_reason"],"yearKey":"jee-main-2021-online-25th-february-evening-slot","active":true},{"question_id":"19nbBbCnM7kQT1i5FF1kltbpb4s","chapter":"compounds-containing-nitrogen","chapterGroup":"organic-chemistry","country":"in","difficulty":"easy","exam":"jee-main","examGroup":"jee","languages":["en"],"marks":4,"negMarks":1,"paperTitle":"JEE Main 2021 (Online) 25th February Evening Shift","permalink":"carbylamine-test-is-used-to-detect-the-presence-of-primary-a-jee-main-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-uuxy3va5hv3w3bqb","question":{"en":{"direction":null,"content":"Carbylamine test is used to detect the presence of primary amino group in an organic compound. Which of the following compound is formed when this test is performed with aniline?","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"<img src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1klteu3tj/9695a5ed-ef36-4f6a-a1ef-ebe9732f63fe/1f240e70-7c1b-11eb-b0eb-7d97e0807144/file-1klteu3tk-107w.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Main 2021 (Online) 25th February Evening Shift Chemistry - Compounds Containing Nitrogen Question 182 English Option 1\">"},{"identifier":"B","content":"<img src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1kltetw7w/72c98f9c-a88a-4992-90d2-6c95667b56f0/1944e9c0-7c1b-11eb-b0eb-7d97e0807144/file-1kltetw7x-137w.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Main 2021 (Online) 25th February Evening Shift Chemistry - Compounds Containi